PAL      TITLE 'MAILPAL     Columbia Univ Network MAILER (Rel. 2)      *
               Address-List Parser'
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*                                                                   *
*        Columbia University Network MAILER  -  Release 2           *
*                                                                   *
*        Program property of Columbia University                    *
*                                                                   *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         SPACE ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*                                                                   *
* Module Name:                                                      *
*                                                                   *
*        MAILPAL                                                    *
*                                                                   *
* Function:                                                         *
*                                                                   *
*        Parser for lists of addresses like those found             *
*        in the RFC822 To: field.                                   *
*                                                                   *
* Attributes:                                                       *
*                                                                   *
*        Reentrant                                                  *
*                                                                   *
*                                                                   *
* Entry Points:                                                     *
*                                                                   *
*        PRSAL                                                      *
*                                                                   *
* Entry Conditions:                                                 *
*                                                                   *
*        R1    = A(PARMS)    see PARMS DSECT,  below                *
*        R15   = A(PRSAL)                                           *
*        R14   = return address                                     *
*        R13   = register save area                                 *
*                                                                   *
* Sample Invocation:                                                *
*                                                                   *
*        CALL PRSAL,(STR,LEN,STK,SLEN,TOK,PAR)                      *
*              str - address of pointer to input string             *
*              len - address of length of input string              *
*              stk - address of stack pointer                       *
*              slen - address of stack length                       *
*              tok - address of token list pointer (output)         *
*              par - address of parse list pointer (output)         *
*                                                                   *
* Exit Conditions:                                                  *
*                                                                   *
*        Normal                                                     *
*                                                                   *
*              R15 = 0       Parse completed successfully.  TOK and *
*                            PAR filled with pointers to results,   *
*                            STK, SLEN, STR, LEN updated.           *
*                                                                   *
*        Error                                                      *
*                                                                   *
*              R15 = 24      Stack overflow,  STR, LEN, STK, SLEN   *
*                            updated.  TOK or PAR may be updated.   *
*              R15 = other   Return codes from LRPARSE and LEX822.  *
*                                                                   *
* Calls to other routines, macros, etc:                             *
*                                                                   *
*        LRPARSE             Table driven parser                    *
*        LEX822              Lexical tokenizer                      *
*        WRTERM              Write to terminal (debugging)          *
*        LINEDIT             Write to terminal (debugging)          *
*        WAITT               Wait for terminal (debugging)          *
*        RFC822 COPY         Tables generated by PAT table generator*
*                                                                   *
* External References:                                              *
*                                                                   *
*        None                                                       *
*                                                                   *
* Work Areas:                                                       *
*                                                                   *
*        LOCALS DSECT        Allocated from stack                   *
*                                                                   *
* Operation:                                                        *
*                                                                   *
*        1) Allocate LOCAL variables storage from stack passed      *
*           as argument.                                            *
*        2) Set up parameter lists for subroutines, etc. in LOCALS. *
*        3) Call LRPARSE,  with RFC822 grammar tables as argument   *
*           (see lable PATTBL,  below).                             *
*                                                                   *
*        LRPARSE,  in the process of parsing,  will call the local  *
*        subroutines that follow the main program,  below:          *
*                                                                   *
*        LEX:                                                       *
*              1) Call the actual tokenizer, LEX822.                *
*              2) Link returned token into TOK chain pointed to     *
*                 by TOKHEAD and TOKLAST in LOCALS.                 *
*              3) If the token returned is a comment token,  call   *
*                 LEX822 again and repeat until a non-comment token *
*                 is returned.                                      *
*              4) If the LEX822 returns end-of-string return code,  *
*                 return EOS token code (zero).                     *
*              5) For other error returns from LEX822,  just pass   *
*                 the code along to caller.                         *
*                                                                   *
*        Semantic routines:                                         *
*              The names of the semantic routines are in the table  *
*              passed to LRPARSE.  See RFC822 COPY for the grammar  *
*              and what reduction causes the semantic routine to    *
*              be called.  The general action of the semantic       *
*              routines is to take the values of previous reductions*
*              off the semantic stack and build the TOK, NODE, and  *
*              MBOX control blocks.                                 *
*                                                                   *
*        All semantic routines and LEX are passed the address of    *
*        LOCALS dsect in R1 so that they can communicate through    *
*        those variables.  In addition,  R0 contains the current    *
*        value of the parser stack pointer for the semantics.       *
*                                                                   *
*        Resulting control block structures from a successful       *
*        parse look something like this:                            *
*                                                                   *
*                            +---------+         +---------+        *
*                            | MBOX 1  |-->...-->| MBOX n  |        *
*                            +---------+         +---------+        *
*        MBXRTL                |  |  |      MBXDML                  *
*     +------------------------+  |  +-----------------+            *
*     |                           | MBXLCL             |            *
*     |                           +------+             |            *
*     V   (route list nodes)             V             V            *
*  +---------+     +---------+     +---------+     +---------+      *
*  | NODE    |---->| NODE    |     | NODE    |     | NODE    |      *
*  +---------+     +---------+     +---------+     +---------+      *
*     |                |                |              |            *
*     V                V                V              V            *
*  +---------+     +---------+     +---------+     +---------+      *
*  | NODE    |     | NODE    |     | TOKEND  |     | TOKEND  |      *
*  +---------+     +---------+     +---------+     +---------+      *
*     |                |                 |               |          *
*     V                V                 |               |          *
*  +---------+     +---------+           |               |          *
*  | TOKEND  |     | TOKEND  |           |               |          *
*  +---------+     +---------+           |               |          *
*    |                |                  |               |          *
*    V                V                  V               V          *
* < @A         ,     @B         :     USERID    @     DOMAIN     >  *
*                                                                   *
*        Basically,  the lowest level is a linked list of all       *
*        tokens seen on input.  Each token gets a TOKEND block which*
*        points to the actual text of the token and contains its    *
*        lexical type (i.e. ATOM, Quoted-String, Comment, etc.).    *
*                                                                   *
*        The NODE block indicates a NODE in the parse tree.  Each   *
*        NODE has a left and right neighbor and a child.  In the    *
*        case of a local-part or domain,  one NODE is allocated for *
*        each significant token and is set to point down to the     *
*        TOKEND block for that token.  In this way, a linked list of*
*        NODEs is used to represent a list of tokens in a local     *
*        part or domain.  For example,  the domain, "CUVMB.BITNET"  *
*        contains three tokens: "CUVMA", ".", "BITNET" but causes   *
*        only two NODEs to be allocated,  pointing to "CUVMA" and   *
*        "BITNET", respectively.  The head of this list of nodes    *
*        is then put in the MBXDML domain list pointer in the MBOX. *
*                                                                   *
*        A route list has an added level of indirection since a     *
*        route list is a list of domains,  where each domain is     *
*        a list of NODEs pointing to TOKs.                          *
*                                                                   *
* Alan Crosswell,  12/83                                            *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        Local Macros                                               *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         MACRO
&LABEL   DEBUG &MSG
         GBLA  &DODEBUG
         AIF   (&DODEBUG).DB01
         MEXIT
.DB01    ANOP
&LABEL   WRTERM &MSG
         WAITT ,
         MEND
         MACRO ,
&LABEL   SEMENTRY
&LABEL   DS    0H            &LABEL semantic routine
         STM   R14,R12,12(R13) save caller's registers
         LR    SP,R0         get stack pointer
         LR    R11,R1        address of LOCALS
         USING LOCALS,R11    address LOCALS
         LR    R12,R15       get base address
         USING &LABEL,R12    tell assembler
         ST    R13,COMMSAVE+4 save in the community save area
         LA    R13,COMMSAVE  and make this be my save area
         DEBUG '&LABEL'      print my name when debugging
         MEND  ,
         MACRO  ,
&LABEL   SEMEXIT
&LABEL   L     R13,4(R13)    restore R13
         L     R14,12(R13)   restore 14
         LM    R0,R12,20(R13) and 0-12; 15 gets error code
         BR    R14           return to caller
         DROP  R11           done with LOCALS
         DROP  R12           done with code
         LTORG ,             literal pool
         MEND  ,
         GBLA  &DODEBUG
&DODEBUG SETA  0             1 for debugging
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        define entries to semantics when debugging                 *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         AIF   (NOT &DODEBUG).DB00
         ENTRY SHIFTSEM
         ENTRY SEMSP1
         ENTRY SEMSP2
         ENTRY SEMLST1
         ENTRY SEMLST2
         ENTRY SEMRTL1
         ENTRY SEMRTL2
         ENTRY SEMADS1
         ENTRY SEMADS2
         ENTRY SEMRADDR
         ENTRY SEMMBOXL
         ENTRY SEMADDRL
         ENTRY SEMGOAL
.DB00    ANOP
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        Parameters                                                 *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
PARMS    DSECT ,             parameters
@STR     DS    A             address of string pointer
@LEN     DS    A             address of string length
@STK     DS    A             address of stack pointer
@SLEN    DS    A             address of stack length
@TOK     DS    A             address of anchor of token list
@PAR     DS    A             address of anchor of canonical addr list
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        Local dynamic variables                                    *
*                                                                   *
*        A register save area and local variables are allocated     *
*        from the high end of the stack.  R13 is used as the base   *
*        of this area so that programs called by this one see       *
*        standard OS linkage.                                       *
*                                                                   *
*        The low end of the stack is where the semantics build the  *
*        TOKEND and MBOX data structures.                           *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
LOCALS   DSECT ,             local variables
         DS    18F           register save area
COMMSAVE DS    18F           common save area used by semantics
STACK    DS    A             address of stack
STKSIZ   DS    F             length
PLIST    DS    A             main plist pointer
TOKHEAD  DS    A             head of token list
TOKLAST  DS    A             last token added to list
MBXHEAD  DS    A             head of canonical address list
SEMERROR DS    F             indication of parse error
*------- parameter list for LEX822 ---------------------------------*
LEXPLIST DS    0F            LEX822 parameter list
LEX@STR  DS    A             address of string pointer
LEX@LEN  DS    A             address of string length
LEX@TTYP DS    A             address of token type
LEX@TPTR DS    A             address of token to fill in
LEX@TLEN DS    A             address of token length to fill in
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
LEXTTYPE DS    F             token type code returned by LEX
*------- parameter list for LRPARSE --------------------------------*
LRPLIST  DS    0F            plist for lrparse
LR@TAB   DS    A             address of table
LR@STK   DS    A             address of stack pointer
LR@LEN   DS    A             address of stack length
LR@COMM  DS    A             address of communications area
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
LRSTK    DS    200F          work area (stack) used by LRPARSE
LLRSTK   EQU   *-LRSTK       lenght of it
LRSTKA   DS    A             pointer to stack
LRLEN    DS    F             length of stack
SSTACK   DS    200F          semantic stack
         DS    0D            keep stack dword aligned
LOCSIZE  EQU   *-LOCALS      length of this dsect
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        Control block definitions                                  *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         SPACE ,
         BLOCKS ,
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
* Register definitions:                                             *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         SPACE ,
R0       EQU   0             work
R1       EQU   1             work
T1       EQU   R1            temporary used by array macros
R2       EQU   2
T2       EQU   R2            temporary used by array macros
R3       EQU   3
SP       EQU   4             semantic stack pointer
R5       EQU   5
R6       EQU   6
R7       EQU   7
R8       EQU   8
R9       EQU   9             TOKEND block base
R10      EQU   10
R11      EQU   11
R12      EQU   12            program base
R13      EQU   13            local variables base
R14      EQU   14
R15      EQU   15
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        Main program                                               *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         SPACE ,
MAILPAL  CSECT ,
PRSAL    MENTRY ,
         ST    R2,STKSIZ     remainder of stack for structures
         ST    R15,STACK     address of that stack
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        set up parameter lists and other initialized locals        *
*        for the LRPARSE and LEX822 routines.                       *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         USING PARMS,R1      look at parameter list
         L     R2,@STR       address of string pointer
         ST    R2,LEX@STR    pass along to lexical routine
         L     R2,@LEN       address of string length
         ST    R2,LEX@LEN    also pass along
         LA    R2,LEXTTYPE   temporary to receive token type
         ST    R2,LEX@TTYP   into plist
         ST    R1,PLIST      keep this in a convenient place
         DROP  R1            done with plist for now
         LA    R2,PATTBL     address of grammar table
         ST    R2,LR@TAB     into LRPARSE's plist
         LA    R2,LRSTK      stack for LRPARSE
         ST    R2,LRSTKA     into pointer
         LA    R2,LRSTKA     address of pointer
         ST    R2,LR@STK     into plist
         LA    R2,LLRSTK     length of the stack
         ST    R2,LRLEN      into plist
         LA    R2,LRLEN      address of length of stack
         ST    R2,LR@LEN     into plist
         ST    R13,LR@COMM   communications area == locals area
         SPACE ,
         XC    TOKHEAD,TOKHEAD initialize token list to empty
         XC    TOKLAST,TOKLAST "
         XC    MBXHEAD,MBXHEAD ditto for canonical address list
         XC    SEMERROR,SEMERROR no semantic error yet.
         SPACE ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        Call LRPARSE                                               *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         LA    R1,LRPLIST    point to the parameter list
         L     R15,=V(LRPARSE) address of the parser
         BALR  R14,R15       call it
         L     R1,PLIST      get handle on plist again
         USING PARMS,R1      get addressability
         L     R2,@TOK       get pointer to token list result
         L     R3,TOKHEAD    get head of token list
         ST    R3,0(R2)      return token list head to caller
         L     R2,@PAR       do likewise for parse list
         L     R3,MBXHEAD    canonical list head
         ST    R3,0(R2)      ...
         L     R2,@STK       ditto for updated stack pointer
         L     R3,STACK      get stack pointer
         ST    R3,0(R2)      return updated stack to caller
         L     R2,@SLEN      stack length
         L     R3,STKSIZ     size
         LA    R3,LOCSIZE(R3) add length of LOCALS
         ST    R3,0(R2)      this is new remaining stack length
         DROP  R1            done with PARMS
         SPACE ,
         LTR   R15,R15       check for parse error
         BNZ   RET1          parse error
         L     R15,SEMERROR  else,  check for semantic error
RET1     EQU   *
         MPEND ,             return via MENTRY macro
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        Parse table generated by PAT                               *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         SPACE ,
PATTBL   DS    0D
         COPY  RFC822        copy in the output of PAT/LALR
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        LEX                                                        *
*                                                                   *
*        This is the lexical analyzer,  LEX.  It calls LEX822 which *
*        does the real work.                                        *
*        on entry,  r1->locals                                      *
*              1) allocate a TOKEND block and set LEXPLIST ptrs to it*
*              2) Call lex822. If the token is a comment,  call     *
*                 LEX822 again until a non-white space token is seen*
*              3) Return the token code expected by LRPARSE in r1.  *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
LEX      DS    0H            Lexical analyzer
         STM   R14,R12,12(R13) save caller's registers
         LR    R11,R1        copy handle on LOCALS
         USING LOCALS,R11    get addressability on it
         LR    R12,R15       get my base address
         USING LEX,R12       establish addressability
         ST    R13,COMMSAVE+4 save it for later
         LA    R13,COMMSAVE  common save area shared with semantics
LEX#0    EQU   *             here if token was white space
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        1) Allocate TOKEND block from stack space.                 *
*          1a) if the first token allocated,  also set TOKHEAD ptr. *
*          1b) if 2nd-nth token,  don't set TOKHEAD, but set TOKNEXT*
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         L     R1,STACK      get stack pointer
         L     R2,STKSIZ     length of stack
         S     R2,=A(TOKSIZ) subtract length of token
         BL    LEX#NOS       no room on the stack for token
         LR    R8,R1         get handle on the token
         LA    R1,TOKSIZ(R1) bump the stack pointer
         ST    R1,STACK      and put it back
         ST    R2,STKSIZ     store back updated size
         XC    0(TOKSIZ,R8),0(R8)  Zero new TOKEND
         ICM   R9,B'1111',TOKLAST get address of last token in list
         BNZ   LEX#1         already is a last token.
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        1a) First call.  the TOKHEAD and TOKLAST pointers          *
*        have to be set up.                                         *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         ST    R8,TOKHEAD    the head of the TOKEND list
         ST    R8,TOKLAST    is also the tail
         USING TOKEND,R8    address the TOK
         XC    TOKPREV,TOKPREV there is no previous
         XC    TOKNEXT,TOKNEXT and no next
         DROP  R8            done with 8 as the base
         LR    R9,R8         get into the standard pointer
         B     LEX#2         and skip to the common code
         SPACE ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        1b) Later call,  set TOKNEXT.                              *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
LEX#1    EQU   *             here when not the first token.
         USING TOKEND,R9    address it
         ST    R8,TOKNEXT    set next pointer in the last token
         ST    R8,TOKLAST    new tail of token list
         DROP  R9            stop looking at last token
         USING TOKEND,R8    look at the new token
         ST    R9,TOKPREV    chain back to prev token
         LR    R9,R8         get 9 back as the token base
         DROP  R8            drop 8 as the token base
LEX#2    EQU   *             common to both 1st and following token
         USING TOKEND,R9    back to 9 as the base
         LA    R1,TOKPTR     where to put address of token string
         ST    R1,LEX@TPTR   into LEX822 plist
         LA    R1,TOKLEN     where to put length of token string
         ST    R1,LEX@TLEN   into LEX822 plist
* (LEX@TTYP, LEX@STR, LEX@LEN pointers are filled in main code)     *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        2) Call LEX822                                             *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         LA    R1,LEXPLIST   plist for LEX822
         L     R15,=V(LEX822) address of the real lexical scanner
         BALR  R14,R15       call it.
         C     R15,=F'4'     check for error return code
         BH    LEX#3         anything >4 is fatal
         SR    R15,R15       0, 4 are OK
         L     R1,LEXTTYPE   get the returned token type into 1
         STC   R1,TOKTYPE    store into token type byte
         CLI   TOKTYPE,C'('  is it a comment?
         BE    LEX#0         loop back for a non-whsp token
         DROP  R9            no longer need TOKEND block base
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        3) Return,  token type in 1,  return code in 15 for errors *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
LEX#R    EQU   *             return
         AIF (NOT &DODEBUG).DB02
         LR    R5,R1         debug
         LINEDIT TEXT='LEX: .........',SUB=(DEC,(R5))
         LR    R1,R5
.DB02    ANOP
         L     R13,4(R13)    and start the long trip home...
         L     R14,12(R13)   restore 14
         L     R0,20(R13)    restore 0
         LM    R2,R12,28(R13) 2-12; 1 contains token code
         BR    R14           return to caller
LEX#3    EQU   *             fatal error from lex822
         ST    R15,SEMERROR  set parse error indication
         SR    R1,R1         return EOS token code
         B     LEX#R         and return
LEX#NOS  EQU   *             no room on the stack
         LA    R15,24        error retcode
         ST    R15,SEMERROR  set parse error
         B     LEX#R         and return
         DROP  R11           done with LOCALS base
         DROP  R12           ditto for code base
         SPACE ,
         LTORG ,
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        SHIFTSEM                                                   *
*                                                                   *
*        Shiftsem shifts the current token onto the semantic stack. *
*        on entry: r0 = SP,  r1 -> LOCALS.                          *
*              1) Put address of last allocated TOKEND block on stack*
*                 SSTACK[SP] := TOKLAST                             *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
SHIFTSEM SEMENTRY ,          shift semantic routine
         L     R3,TOKLAST    address of last token seen
         STARR R3,SSTACK,SP  onto semantic stack
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         SEMEXIT ,
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        NULL, SP1, SP2                                             *
*                                                                   *
*        Null, SP1, SP2 each just copy a value from the semantic    *
*        stack.  Null copies SP+0 (does nothing),  SP1 copies SP+1, *
*        and SP2 copies SP+2.                                       *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         AIF   (&DODEBUG).DB03
SEMNULL  EQU   0             Normally does nothing
         AGO   .DB04
.DB03    ANOP
SEMNULL  SEMENTRY ,          when debugging,  print our name
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         SEMEXIT ,
.DB04    ANOP
SEMSP1   SEMENTRY ,          SP1 semantic routine
         LDARR R3,SSTACK+4,SP SSTACK[SP+1]
         STARR R3,SSTACK,SP  SSTACK[SP] := SSTACK[SP+1]
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         SEMEXIT ,
SEMSP2   SEMENTRY ,          SP2 semantic routine
         LDARR R3,SSTACK+8,SP SSTACK[SP+2]
         STARR R3,SSTACK,SP  SSTACK[SP] := SSTACK[SP+2]
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         SEMEXIT ,
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        ZERO                                                       *
*                                                                   *
*        Zero returns zero on the semantic stack.                   *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
SEMZERO  SEMENTRY ,          ZERO semantic
         SR    R3,R3         get a zero
         STARR R3,SSTACK,SP  put it on the stack
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         SEMEXIT ,
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        LST1, LST2                                                 *
*                                                                   *
*        Both domains and local-parts consist of lists of token     *
*        that may be separated by other "white space" tokens        *
*        like comments.  A NODE block is allocated for each token   *
*        which points down to the actual TOKEND block.  The next    *
*        and prev pointers of the NODE link the list together.      *
*        LST1 allocates a new NODE block and sets up the necessary  *
*        pointers and LST2 allocates a NODE block for the <word>    *
*        and links it to the NODE block already on the stack.       *
*                                                                   *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
SEMLST1  SEMENTRY ,          LST1 semantic routine
         L     R1,STACK      get stack pointer
         L     R2,STKSIZ     get remaining length of stack memory
         S     R2,=A(NODSIZ) minus size of a node
         BL    LST1#NOS      no stack space.
         LR    R8,R1         copy the pointer
         LA    R1,NODSIZ(R1) bump stack pointer
         ST    R1,STACK      save it back
         ST    R2,STKSIZ     ditto for stack size
         USING NODE,R8       address the node
         LDARR R3,SSTACK,SP  sstack[sp] -> TOKEND block
         ST    R3,NODDOWN    set the down pointer with this
         XC    NODNEXT,NODNEXT no left or right
         XC    NODPREV,NODPREV neighbors at this point
         DROP  R8            done looking at NODE
         STARR R8,SSTACK,SP  return address of node on sem stack
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         B     LST1#R        return
LST1#NOS EQU   *             no stack space
         LA    R15,24
         ST    R15,SEMERROR  set parse error
LST1#R   SEMEXIT ,           return
         SPACE 3
SEMLST2  SEMENTRY ,          LST2 semantic routine
         L     R1,STACK      get stack pointer
         L     R2,STKSIZ     get remaining length of stack memory
         S     R2,=A(NODSIZ) minus size of a node
         BL    LST2#NOS      no stack space.
         LR    R8,R1         copy the pointer
         LA    R1,NODSIZ(R1) bump stack pointer
         ST    R1,STACK      save it back
         ST    R2,STKSIZ     ditto for stack size
         USING NODE,R8       address the node
         LDARR R6,SSTACK+8,SP  sstack[sp+2] -> TOKEND block
         LDARR R5,SSTACK,SP  one NODE is at SP
         ST    R6,NODDOWN    set the down pointer with this
         XC    NODNEXT,NODNEXT no next node
         ST    R5,NODPREV    the first is PREV
         DROP  R8            done with NODE
         USING NODE,R5       address the first one
         ST    R8,NODNEXT    the second is NEXT
         DROP  R5
         STARR R8,SSTACK,SP  return address of second on stack
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         B     LST2#R        return
LST2#NOS EQU   *             no space on stack
         LA    R15,24
         ST    R15,SEMERROR  set error
LST2#R   SEMEXIT ,
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        RTL1, RTL2                                                 *
*                                                                   *
*        A route lists is a list of domain lists.  RTL1 and RTL2    *
*        build lists of NODEs that point to the domain list NODEs   *
*        in much the same way that LST1 and LST2 point to TOKens.   *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
SEMRTL1  SEMENTRY ,          RTL1 semantic routine
         L     R1,STACK      get stack pointer
         L     R2,STKSIZ     get remaining length of stack memory
         S     R2,=A(NODSIZ) minus size of a node
         BL    RTL1#NOS      no stack space.
         LR    R8,R1         copy the pointer
         LA    R1,NODSIZ(R1) bump stack pointer
         ST    R1,STACK      save it back
         ST    R2,STKSIZ     ditto for stack size
         LDARR R3,SSTACK+4,SP sstack[sp+1] -> last NODE block
         USING NODE,R3       address the domain node
RTL1#1   EQU   *             loop to search for 1st NODE
         CLC   =F'0',NODPREV is this the 1st node?
         BE    RTL1#2        yes,  break out of loop
         L     R3,NODPREV    chain back
         B     RTL1#1        and loop
         DROP  R3            done with NODE
RTL1#2   EQU   *             here when head of list found
         USING NODE,R8       address the node
         ST    R3,NODDOWN    set the down pointer with this
         XC    NODNEXT,NODNEXT no left or right
         XC    NODPREV,NODPREV neighbors at this point
         DROP  R8            done looking at NODE
         STARR R8,SSTACK,SP  return address of node on sem stack
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         B     RTL1#R        return
RTL1#NOS EQU   *             out of stack space
         LA    R15,24
         ST    R15,SEMERROR  set error code
RTL1#R   SEMEXIT ,
         SPACE 3
SEMRTL2  SEMENTRY ,          RTL2 semantic routine
         L     R1,STACK      get stack pointer
         L     R2,STKSIZ     get remaining length of stack memory
         S     R2,=A(NODSIZ) minus size of a node
         BL    RTL2#NOS      no stack space.
         LR    R8,R1         copy the pointer
         LA    R1,NODSIZ(R1) bump stack pointer
         ST    R1,STACK      save it back
         ST    R2,STKSIZ     ditto for stack size
         LDARR R6,SSTACK+12,SP sstack[sp+3] -> last domain NODE block
         USING NODE,R6       address the domain node
RTL2#1   EQU   *             loop to find head of domain list
         CLC   =F'0',NODPREV is this the head of the list?
         BE    RTL2#2        yes
         L     R6,NODPREV    chain back
         B     RTL2#1        and itterate
RTL2#2   EQU   *             here when head of domain list found.
         DROP  R6            done with NODE
         LDARR R5,SSTACK,SP  one route NODE is at SP
         USING NODE,R8       address the node
         ST    R6,NODDOWN    set the down pointer with this
         XC    NODNEXT,NODNEXT no next node
         ST    R5,NODPREV    the first is PREV
         DROP  R8            done with NODE
         USING NODE,R5       address the first one
         ST    R8,NODNEXT    the second is NEXT
         DROP  R5
         STARR R8,SSTACK,SP  return address of second on stack
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         B     RTL2#R        return
RTL2#NOS EQU   *             no stack space left
         LA    R15,24
         ST    R15,SEMERROR  set error
RTL2#R   SEMEXIT ,
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        ADS1, ADS2                                                 *
*                                                                   *
*        ADS1 allocates a MBOX block from the stack and fills it    *
*        with the local-part and domain pointers after following    *
*        them back to their respective head NODEs.  ADS2 is ADS1    *
*        with domain set to zero.                                   *
*        on entry: r0 = SP,  r1 -> LOCALS.                          *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
SEMADS1  SEMENTRY ,          ADS1 semantic routine
         L     R1,STACK      get stack pointer
         L     R2,STKSIZ     remaining size of stack
         S     R2,=A(MBXSIZ) size of a MBOX bloc
         BL    ADS1#NOS      stack too small
         LR    R8,R1         copy pointer
         LA    R1,MBXSIZ(R1) increment stack pointer
         ST    R1,STACK      put it back
         ST    R2,STKSIZ     ditto for updated size
         USING MBOX,R8       address the mbox
         XC    0(MBXSIZ,R8),0(R8) zero out the block
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        SStack points to the last added NODE on the local-part     *
*        list.  Follow the PREV pointers back to the first node on  *
*        the list and put the address of the first node into MBXLCL *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         LDARR R5,SSTACK,SP  get local part tail node
         LTR   R5,R5         no local-part?
         BZ    ADS1#1        don't search back then.
         USING NODE,R5       address the NODE structure
ADS1#0   EQU   *             loop to search back for 1st NODE
         CLC   =F'0',NODPREV is this the head of the list?
         BE    ADS1#1        yes,  r5 has the head node address
         L     R5,NODPREV    else,  chain back and iterrate
         B     ADS1#0        back to top of loop
ADS1#1   EQU   *             here when head node is found
         ST    R5,MBXLCL     this is the local-part list
         DROP  R5            done with NODE
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        SStack+2 points to the last added NODE on the domain       *
*        list.  Follow the PREV pointers back to the first node on  *
*        the list and put the address of the first node into MBXDML *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         LDARR R5,SSTACK+8,SP get domain tail node
         LTR   R5,R5         no domain?
         BZ    ADS1#3        don't search back then.
         USING NODE,R5       address the NODE structure
ADS1#2   EQU   *             loop to search back for 1st NODE
         CLC   =F'0',NODPREV is this the head of the list?
         BE    ADS1#3        yes,  r5 has the head node address
         L     R5,NODPREV    else,  chain back and iterrate
         B     ADS1#2        back to top of loop
ADS1#3   EQU   *             here when head node is found
         ST    R5,MBXDML     this is the domain list
         DROP  R5            done with NODE
         STARR R8,SSTACK,SP  return address of MBOX on stack
         DROP  R8            done with MBOX base
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         B     ADS1#R        return
ADS1#NOS EQU   *             no stack space
         LA    R15,24        error code
         ST    R15,SEMERROR  set error flag
ADS1#R   SEMEXIT ,
SEMADS2  SEMENTRY ,          ADS2 semantic routine
         L     R1,STACK      get stack pointer
         L     R2,STKSIZ     remaining size of stack
         S     R2,=A(MBXSIZ) size of a MBOX bloc
         BL    ADS2#NOS      stack too small
         LR    R8,R1         copy pointer
         LA    R1,MBXSIZ(R1) increment stack pointer
         ST    R1,STACK      put it back
         ST    R2,STKSIZ     ditto for updated size
         USING MBOX,R8       address the mbox
         XC    0(MBXSIZ,R8),0(R8) zero out the block
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        SStack points to the last added NODE on the local-part     *
*        list.  Follow the PREV pointers back to the first node on  *
*        the list and put the address of the first node into MBXLCL *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         LDARR R5,SSTACK,SP  get local part tail node
         LTR   R5,R5         no local-part?
         BZ    ADS2#1        don't search back then.
         USING NODE,R5       address the NODE structure
ADS2#0   EQU   *             loop to search back for 1st NODE
         CLC   =F'0',NODPREV is this the head of the list?
         BE    ADS2#1        yes,  r5 has the head node address
         L     R5,NODPREV    else,  chain back and iterrate
         B     ADS2#0        back to top of loop
ADS2#1   EQU   *             here when head node is found
         ST    R5,MBXLCL     this is the local-part list
         DROP  R5            done with NODE
         DROP  R8            done with MBOX
         STARR R8,SSTACK,SP  return MBOX address on stack
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         B     ADS2#R        return
ADS2#NOS EQU   *             no space on stack
         LA    R15,24
         ST    R15,SEMERROR  set error code
ADS2#R   SEMEXIT ,
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        RADDR                                                      *
*                                                                   *
*        RADDR is similar to ADS2.  It gets the head of the route   *
*        list and plugs it into MBXRTL.  The address of the MBOX is *
*        passed on the stack at SP+2 (addr_spec) and the address of *
*        the last element in the route is at SP.                    *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
SEMRADDR SEMENTRY ,          RADDR semantic routine
         LDARR R8,SSTACK+8,SP get address of MBOX
         USING MBOX,R8       address it
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        SStack+2 points to the last added NODE on the route        *
*        list.  Follow the PREV pointers back to the first node on  *
*        the list and put the address of the first node into MBXRTL *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
         LDARR R5,SSTACK+4,SP get route tail node
         LTR   R5,R5         no route?
         BZ    RADDR#1       don't search back then.
         USING NODE,R5       address the NODE structure
RADDR#0  EQU   *             loop to search back for 1st NODE
         CLC   =F'0',NODPREV is this the head of the list?
         BE    RADDR#1       yes,  r5 has the head node address
         L     R5,NODPREV    else,  chain back and iterrate
         B     RADDR#0       back to top of loop
RADDR#1  EQU   *             here when head node is found
         ST    R5,MBXRTL     this is the route list
         STARR R8,SSTACK,SP  return address of MBOX on stack
         DROP  R5            done with NODE
         DROP  R8            done with MBOX
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         SEMEXIT ,
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        MBOXL                                                      *
*                                                                   *
*        MBOXL chains one MBOX onto the end of the list of MBOX's   *
*        The new MBOX is at SP+2 and the list is at SP. Either      *
*        one may be a null pointer.  Check for this case.           *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
SEMMBOXL SEMENTRY ,          MBOXL semantic routine
         LDARR R5,SSTACK,SP  one MBOX is at SP
         LDARR R6,SSTACK+8,SP other is at SP+2
         LTR   R5,R5         check for a null pointer
         BZ    MBOXL#R       it is;  return pointer to other
         LTR   R6,R6         ditto for 2nd pointer
         BZ    MBOXL#1       return pointer to other
         USING MBOX,R5       address the first one
         ST    R6,MBXNEXT    the second is NEXT
         DROP  R5
         USING MBOX,R6       address the second one
         ST    R5,MBXPREV    the first is PREV
         DROP  R6
         B     MBOXL#R       return
MBOXL#1  EQU   *             here when pointer is null
         LR    R6,R5         get other ptr into result reg
MBOXL#R  EQU   *             here for return or null pointer
         STARR R6,SSTACK,SP  return address of second on stack
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         SEMEXIT ,
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        ADDRL                                                      *
*                                                                   *
*        ADDRL concatenates two address lists.  At SP is the        *
*        address of the last MBOX of one list.  At SP+2 is the      *
*        address of the tail of the other.  The tail of list1 is    *
*        linked to the head of list2 and tail of list2 is returned  *
*        on the stack. Either one of list1 or list2 may be a null   *
*        pointer if it was passed on the stack from a null rule.    *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
SEMADDRL SEMENTRY ,          ADDRL semantic routine
         LDARR R5,SSTACK,SP   one MBOX is at SP
         LDARR R6,SSTACK+8,SP other is at SP+2
         LTR   R5,R5         see if list1 is a null pointer
         BZ    ADDRL#R       it is;  return list2 (even if null)
         LTR   R6,R6         ditto for list2
         BZ    ADDRL#2       it is;  return list1
         LR    R7,R6         copy pointer to tail of list2
         USING MBOX,R7       use this copy to find the head
ADDRL#0  EQU   *             loop to find head of list2
         CLC   =F'0',MBXPREV are we at the head?
         BE    ADDRL#1       yes,  out of loop
         L     R7,MBXPREV    get prev pointer
         B     ADDRL#0       and iterrate
ADDRL#1  EQU   *             here when head of list2 is found
         ST    R5,MBXPREV    point list2 back at tail of list1
         DROP  R7            done with head of list2
         USING MBOX,R5       talk about tail of list1 now
         ST    R7,MBXNEXT    point list1 tail forward to head of list2
         DROP  R5            done talking about list1
         B     ADDRL#R       return
ADDRL#2  EQU   *             here when list2 is null
         LR    R6,R5         use list1 pointer
ADDRL#R  EQU   *             here to return or bypass for null ptr
         STARR R6,SSTACK,SP  return address of tail of list2
         SR    R15,R15       zero retcode
         SEMEXIT ,
         EJECT ,
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
*        GOAL                                                       *
*                                                                   *
*        The goal is achieved!  SP has the address of the last      *
*        MBOX in address-list.  Find the head of the list and put   *
*        it into MBXHEAD.  Set a non-zero return code to cause the  *
*        parser to return.                                          *
*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
SEMGOAL  SEMENTRY ,          GOAL semantic routine
         LDARR R5,SSTACK,SP   tail MBOX is at SP
         LTR   R5,R5         see if all reductions were null
         BZ    GOAL#1        yes,  return an empty mbox list.
         USING MBOX,R5       address the mbox
GOAL#0   EQU   *             loop here searching for head of list
         CLC   =F'0',MBXPREV look for a prev pointer
         BE    GOAL#1        found the head of the list
         L     R5,MBXPREV    chain back
         B     GOAL#0        iterrate
GOAL#1   EQU   *             here when head of list is found
         ST    R5,MBXHEAD    set head pointer
         DROP  R5            done with MBOX
         LA    R15,1         non-zero to indicate end of parse
         SEMEXIT ,
         END   ,
